facts:
The area model for $2 \times 2$ digits gives **four** part-products.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\small}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,3);
\draw (3,0)--(3,3);
\draw (0,1.5)--(5,1.5);
\node[above] at (1.5,3) {tens};
\node[above] at (4,3) {ones};
\node[left] at (0,2.25) {tens};
\node[left] at (0,0.75) {ones};
\node at (1.5,2.25) {part-product};
\node at (4,2.25) {part-product};
\node at (1.5,0.75) {part-product};
\node at (4,0.75) {part-product};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

